{{- /*
  pr_description.user: the Publish-phase prompt for generating one stack
  layer's PR body from structured signals (feature context, the layer's
  position/title/phases/rationale, the full stack listing, commit bodies,
  diff stat). The raw line-level diff is intentionally NOT injected —
  commit messages + stats are sufficient for description and fit
  comfortably inside CLI prompt budgets even on very large features.

  The reply is body-only markdown: the description session no longer
  produces a title, and the parser treats the whole reply as the body
  (with a lenient fallback stripping a legacy TITLE: marker).
*/ -}}
{{- define "pr_description.user" -}}
# Generate PR Description Body

{{ if or .FeatureName .FeatureDescription }}## Feature

{{ if .FeatureName }}Name: {{ .FeatureName }}

{{ end }}{{ if .FeatureDescription }}{{ .FeatureDescription }}

{{ end }}{{ end }}{{ if .LayerPosition }}## This Layer

Position: Layer {{ .LayerPosition }}{{ if .Stack }} of {{ len .Stack }}{{ end }}
{{ if .LayerTitle }}Title: {{ .LayerTitle }}
{{ end }}{{ if .LayerPhases }}Phases: {{ .LayerPhases }}
{{ end }}{{ if .LayerRationale }}Rationale: {{ .LayerRationale }}
{{ end }}
{{ end }}{{ if .Stack }}## Delivery Stack

This feature delivers as a stack of layered pull requests — one branch and pull request per layer below. The highest position is the top layer. This prompt describes only the layer named above.

{{ $top := 0 }}{{ range .Stack }}{{ if gt .Position $top }}{{ $top = .Position }}{{ end }}{{ end }}{{ range .Stack }}- Layer {{ .Position }}{{ if .Title }}: {{ .Title }}{{ end }}{{ if eq .Position $top }} (top layer){{ end }} — phases {{ .Phases }}{{ if .Branch }}, branch {{ .Branch }}{{ end }}
{{ end }}
{{ end }}{{ if .CommitBodies }}## Commit Messages

```
{{ .CommitBodies }}
```

{{ end }}{{ if .DiffStat }}## Changes (file stats)

```
{{ .DiffStat }}
```

{{ end }}## Instructions

Generate the body of the pull request description for this layer only, using
the feature context, the layer's position, title, phases, and rationale, the
delivery stack listing, the commit messages, and file-level change stats
above. Describe only this layer's changes — not the feature as a whole and
not other layers' changes. The raw line-level diff is intentionally not
included — rely on the commit messages and stats to describe the change.
Use only the context supplied in this prompt. Do not request or invoke tools,
inspect files, run commands, browse the web, delegate work, or ask for more
information. Produce the best complete result possible from the available context.

Produce:
1. A Summary section with 1-3 bullets on what changed in this layer and why
2. A Test plan section

Output the body in markdown only. Do not include a pull request title.
{{ end -}}
